// Language section: Records (the `type` keyword).
page records { sites = [:reference]
  h1 "Records" {}

  p "A `type` declares a named record — a fixed set of named, typed fields. Records describe the shape of values, function parameters, and the backing type of every block." {}

  h2 "Declaring a record type" {}

  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
type Dog {
  name: utf8
  age:  u32
}

let rex = Dog { name: "Rex", age: 4u32 }
WCL
  }

  h2 "extends" {}

  p "A record may `extends` another, inheriting all its fields. The child type is a structural superset; it satisfies any context that accepts the parent." {}
  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
type Dog {
  name: utf8
  age:  u32
}

type Pet extends Dog {
  breed: utf8
}
WCL
  }

  callout "Records and blocks" {
    class = ["note"]
    body  = "A record becomes a block kind when decorated with @block(\"kind\") — see Schema & Decorators. The block's labels then bind positionally to fields marked @inline(N)."
  }

  p "Next: [Interfaces](interfaces)." {}
}
